  "rationale": "Deploy mfa:admin and mfa:dbadmin together. mfa:admin blocks authentication to both DC and ADFS, making admin_dc and admin_adfs unreachable. Consequently, mfa:dbadmin blocks authentication to the database, file server, and backup even if database-admin credentials are stolen, preventing every exfiltration technique. No single control suffices: mfa:admin alone leaves the CI-server secrets route open (stolen_admin bypasses its patch); mfa:dbadmin alone is bypassed through admin_dc or admin_adfs. Any other single control leaves a route through phishing, internal access, Kerberoasting, DC compromise, and database exfiltration. Segmentation alone is bypassed by escalating a phished workstation or laptop."
 },
